  "summary": "All five post-discharge med reconciliations under RBC-TOC-02 are done. Each patient has a progress note, and a correction note was added where something arrived during the work.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide is now 40 mg twice daily (old order mr-00075 replaced by mr-t0001), per the signed addendum. Potassium chloride is stopped, per the discharge summary. Omeprazole is unchanged: pantoprazole was a hospital formulary swap, so it was not ordered. Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin continue unchanged. Lisinopril: I first kept it on hold because his 10/21 potassium was 5.4. A repeat BMP arrived (10/23: potassium 4.7, creatinine 1.21), which meets the discharge condition, so I resumed it (mr-00072). The PCP task I had created (task-t0003, review next potassium) is no longer needed; the tools couldn't cancel it, so please close it. An unsigned draft addendum also arrived proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily. Unsigned addenda don't count under the policy, so I made no change. Notes: doc-t0004, doc-t0019.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): I first raised carvedilol to 12.5 mg twice daily per the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived reversing that (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing), so carvedilol is back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016). Aspirin and insulin 70/30 continue. Two messages flagged to you:\n- Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so I left the order unchanged (comm-t0006).\n- Glipizide 5 mg: filled at an outside pharmacy, prescribed by Dr. Desai. The discharge papers don't mention it, there is no clinic order, and I did not order it (comm-t0007).\nNotes: doc-t0008, doc-t0020.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): I resumed lisinopril 20 mg because creatinine was 1.08 on 10/22 (below the 1.3 condition). A potassium of 5.5 then arrived (10/23), so I put lisinopril back on hold. Task for you, due 10/26: review the next potassium (task-t0018). Both insulins and rosuvastatin continue. Notes: doc-t0010, doc-t0021.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (10/21 creatinine 1.12, below the 1.5 condition; potassium 4.4). Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue. Note: doc-t0012.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER stays on hold. Its only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, which doesn't meet a condition that asks for post-discharge labs. Task for you, due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected (task-t0013). I found no BMP order in our chart, so please make sure it is arranged. Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue. Note: doc-t0014.\n\nI closed the four new inbox items (inbox-a0001 to a0004), with links to the related orders and notes. No other new items came in.",
